    {
      "id": "tutorial-interface-editing-flow-s5",
      "type": "page-section",
      "label": "Check yourself",
      "position": {
        "x": 930,
        "y": 460
      },
      "width": 1100,
      "height": 560,
      "data": {
        "title": "Check yourself",
        "body": "**Challenge**\n\n1. Select a node and explain why it is the right starting point.\n2. Make one deliberate edit in properties.\n3. Add one new thing the graph actually needs.\n4. Connect or place it cleanly.\n5. Verify the graph still makes sense before moving on.\n\n**Checkpoint**\n\nYou are done when you can say:\n- selection comes before editing\n- properties help me inspect current state before I mutate\n- I create and connect things intentionally, not randomly\n- reuse is useful only if the graph remains coherent afterward\n- verification is part of the editing flow, not a separate optional step",
        "presentation": {
          "glyph": {
            "kind": "icon",
            "name": "Article"
          },
          "baseLevel": "detail"
        },
        "identity": {
          "graphId": "tutorial-interface-editing-flow"
        },
